# netsurf: a sheet change while a sheet is in flight is answered against the cascade the boxes hold (patch 443)
# Generated 2026-11-22
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 442)
#
# "sheet change: a sheet is still loading or changing" (3.3 a load on 5
# sites, 442's census) took the full rebuild, mostly in synchronous flushes
# (a script's layout read), which 442's wait cannot reach. But
# html_css_refresh_selection_context refreshes c->select_ctx only once
# every sheet has settled: a full rebuild in that window cascades the very
# context the boxes were cascaded with, and computes the same styles.
# google's case: an inline sheet done while another is in flight.
#
# A selection-context generation makes that checkable: rl_ctx_gen is
# bumped (html_css_ctx_changed) at every change to c->select_ctx -- created,
# refreshed, a sheet removed from it (re-processing, prune), swapped by
# 415's no-op; a box build records the generation it started with
# (rl_build_gen) and, done, the tree's (rl_boxes_gen) only if the context
# did not change meanwhile; 415's no-op records it too; the inherited
# colour path (fresh context) clears it. html_rl_doc_noop answers "sheet
# change" with no rebuild when a sheet is unsettled, nothing was pruned
# and rl_boxes_gen == rl_ctx_gen. The sheet in flight marks when it is
# done, and that re-cascade sees every sheet. A removal or root change is
# not answered this way (their own change is the point).
#
--- a/content/handlers/html/private.h
+++ b/content/handlers/html/private.h
@@ -189,6 +189,13 @@
 	struct html_stylesheet *stylesheets;
 	/**< Style selection context */
